    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d739">

                <pb facs="0837" n="827" sameAs="frus:frus1943v01/pg827"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">550.AD1/16: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Standley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-03-30T13:00:00+03:00">March 30, 1943—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 4:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>222. Department’s 168, March 24, 10 p.m.<anchor n="15" xml:id="d739-f1"/> In a
                    note dated March 29, Molotov states that the Soviet Government does not object
                    to the inclusion of representatives of the Governments of Iceland, Iran,
                    Liberia, and Egypt among those to be invited to the conference.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Standley</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
